Fixing StyleBro's rules and the built-in rules init and migrate turn on (141 ids); --all applies every analyzer's and compiler fix.
Generators: building NCalc.SourceGenerators first (in the default configuration, the one 'dotnet format' loads): the code uses it as a source generator, and without its output the generated code would be missing from the checks.
Held back: IDE0049: this .NET SDK's 'dotnet format' ignores the suppressor StyleBro's multi-target guard uses for IDE rules, so their fixes could write C# or APIs that another target framework or project compiling the same file doesn't have. They aren't applied here; a newer .NET SDK's 'dotnet format' applies them where the guard allows.
Multi-targeted: one 'dotnet format' run per target framework (net10.0, net462, net8.0, netstandard2.0). net8.0: only the projects whose code compiles differently there.
Configurations: runs for Release (NCalc.Parser) too: their code compiles differently there ('#if DEBUG', files or docs of that configuration), and the build of every configuration gets the same fixes and checks.
Shared files: these projects compile the same files with other '#if' symbols or settings, so each group gets a run of its own (loaded together, 'dotnet format' crashes: https://github.com/dotnet/roslyn/issues/86001): NCalc.Core | NCalc.Benchmarks.
Checked net10.0 (run 1 of 6)
Checked net8.0, part 1 of 2 (run 2 of 6)
Checked netstandard2.0 (run 3 of 6)
Checked net462 (run 4 of 6)
Checked net8.0, part 2 of 2 (run 5 of 6)
Checked netstandard2.0, Release (run 6 of 6)
